windfall-stretch is part of Windfall and is licensed under the GNU General
Public License, version 3 or later, like the rest of it.

Parts of it are ported to Rust from the two libraries below. The ported
code is in src/stretcher.rs (the spectral processing: the prediction of
phases along time and along the spectrum, the handling of several
channels, the map of frequencies used for pitch-shifting and the
correction of formants), in src/stft.rs (the self-normalising short-time
Fourier transform and its Kaiser window) and in src/fft.rs (the real FFT
with bins shifted by half a bin). Their licenses ask that the notices
below stay with the code.


